parts.text:
**Findings**
- High: `SettingsActivity.RootPreferencesFragment` was mutating `Preference` state from a background thread, and the About flow was starting `ReportActivity` from that worker thread. I refactored that so settings setup stays on the main thread, plugin visibility uses one helper, and the About navigation is marshaled back to the UI thread in [SettingsActivity.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G005_termux/app/src/main/java/com/termux/app/activities/SettingsActivity.java:52).
- Medium: the settings layer had several static `PreferenceDataStore` singletons that captured a `Context`. That’s unnecessary lifecycle coupling and a leak risk. I replaced that pattern with per-fragment stores and shared setup primitives in [BasePreferenceFragment.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G005_termux/app/src/main/java/com/termux/app/fragments/settings/BasePreferenceFragment.java:11), [BasePreferenceDataStore.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G005_termux/app/src/main/java/com/termux/app/fragments/settings/BasePreferenceDataStore.java:7), and [BaseLogLevelPreferenceDataStore.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G005_termux/app/src/main/java/com/termux/app/fragments/settings/BaseLogLevelPreferenceDataStore.java:5).
- Medium: the five debugging preference screens duplicated the same log-level wiring and local data-store boilerplate. I centralized that in [BaseDebuggingPreferencesFragment.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G005_termux/app/src/main/java/com/termux/app/fragments/settings/BaseDebuggingPreferencesFragment.java:8) and [LogLevelPreferenceUtils.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G005_termux/app/src/main/java/com/termux/app/fragments/settings/LogLevelPreferenceUtils.java:11), then slimmed the concrete fragments such as [termux/DebuggingPreferencesFragment.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G005_termux/app/src/main/java/com/termux/app/fragments/settings/termux/DebuggingPreferencesFragment.java:17), [termux/TerminalIOPreferencesFragment.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G005_termux/app/src/main/java/com/termux/app/fragments/settings/termux/TerminalIOPreferencesFragment.java:15), and [termux/TerminalViewPreferencesFragment.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G005_termux/app/src/main/java/com/termux/app/fragments/settings/termux/TerminalViewPreferencesFragment.java:15).

The refactor removes a large amount of repeated settings code, eliminates the `Context`-holding singleton pattern, and makes the settings package easier to extend safely.

Validation was limited: `./gradlew :app:compileDebugJavaWithJavac --no-daemon` could not run because `gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar` is missing from this checkout, so I could not complete a real compile or test pass.

